// Title: Registry Persistence via Explorer Run Key
// Sigma ID: b7916c2a-fa2f-4795-9477-32b731f70f11
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), oscd.community
// Date: 2018-07-18 | Modified: 2023-12-11
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, T1547.001
// Description: Detects a possible persistence mechanism using RUN key for Windows Explorer and pointing to a
//   suspicious folder
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2018/07/unit42-upatre-continues-evolve-new-anti-analysis-techniques/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_susp_reg_persist_explorer_run.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Explorer\\Run" and (RegistryValueData contains ":\\$Recycle.bin\\" or RegistryValueData contains ":\\ProgramData\\" or RegistryValueData contains ":\\Temp\\" or RegistryValueData contains ":\\Users\\Default\\" or RegistryValueData contains ":\\Users\\Public\\" or RegistryValueData contains ":\\Windows\\Temp\\" or RegistryValueData contains "\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\")
